  unit: { count: 428, covers: "The emulator's guide names the adb the shell found as each host's shell writes it, with where Android Studio puts it behind a ? where none was found; leads each command with its shell, Terminal on macOS; opens on the AVD used last only while none runs, its start command the other way; sends the certificate where su does not answer, the push by hand the other way; sets Android 15's install, Wi-Fi and undo paths apart and undoes the certificate by Trusted credentials then Uninstall and OK; explains its steps behind their ?; offers its request in the emulator only while one runs, Chrome's welcome behind its ?. No emulator running reads not done only from a reading that found none, and a proof still reads done. A step with help and MenuPath flow as text, so the ? follows the last word. The shell names a user CA by OpenSSL's old subject hash (checked against openssl), pushes the DER and writes it as su at the first free or same-bytes index, then announces the change; sets and clears the global proxy on every running emulator; refuses with none running before any command; spells the SDK under $HOME or $env:LOCALAPPDATA and refuses a path its shell would change; finds the AVD used last by its newest launch file and display name; reports no adb as no reading; opens the marked address, the certificate with the installer's screen and Trusted credentials on every running emulator, refuses a mark that is not one, starts the AVD used last and leaves it running, and never takes an AVD from the webview. The harness scripts adb, the SDK, the AVD and each outcome; the walkthrough judge lists W17's findings" }
